---
arrangement: lint-clean-sentence
when-used: The whole quiet-on-clean sentence a findings-free `dorc lint` prints instead of a report. Values, in order: file count, its plural suffix, source count, its plural suffix.
why: 27R section 8 delta-positive-clean-sentence: clean is stated positively, never as silence.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- lint-clean-sentence && mise run loom:promote -- lint-clean-sentence`. `mise run loom:vars -- --all lint-clean-sentence` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- oracle.sh --
# dorc-lang/v0.2
# Nothing here for any lint source to report: the point of the case is the render a CLEAN run
# produces, which is a sentence rather than an empty report.
nginx__is_converged() {
   systemctl is-active --quiet nginx
}

-- replay --
$ dorc lint oracle.sh --no-tools
dorc lint: clean -- nothing found across 1 file, 7 sources.
